# Fixed defect 315, 2026-10-04 (lane b11-parse). Symptom: a member written
# on its head's line over nothing, `variant T: a`, was told twice, the head's
# junk at the `:` and `empty_variant` at the head, where moving the member
# below cures both; `record R: x` the same with `empty_record`. Cause:
# `parse/members_below.no_members_below` told `empty` beside the junk over no
# members below, whatever the junk was (defect 198's repair). Repair: where
# the junk is the members, a `:` and a name or a name and a `:`, the junk's
# report is the one, its words sending them below. Where it is anything else,
# a closer, a number, a word like `extends`, or a bare name, which may be a
# case or a foreign word, the block is empty indeed and both are told, as
# `check/panel-187-a-heads-line-that-goes-on-is-told-once` pins for a closer.

variant One: a  #~ expected_end_of_line

record Two: x  #~ expected_end_of_line

variant Three: a, b  #~ expected_end_of_line

record Four: x: i64  #~ expected_end_of_line

record Five x: i64  #~ expected_end_of_line

variant Six: a(x: i64)  #~ expected_end_of_line

variant Closer )  #~ expected_end_of_line empty_variant

variant Number: 1  #~ expected_end_of_line empty_variant

record Extends Base  #~ expected_end_of_line empty_record

variant Bare a  #~ expected_end_of_line empty_variant

function main()
    print(1)
